# AI Notebook — optional build-time keys
#
# THE APP DOES NOT NEED ANY OF THIS. The normal way to use cloud AI is to open
# Settings -> AI & Providers -> Add provider and paste your own key, which is stored
# encrypted in the Android Keystore and never leaves the device except to the provider
# you chose. Everything below is only for shipping a build that already has a free-tier
# key configured out of the box.
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy the values you want into `local.properties` at the repo root (gitignored),
#      or export them as environment variables before building.
#   2. Rebuild. They are baked into `BuildConfig` in the `:data` module and seeded as a
#      provider named "Groq (built-in)" the first time the app runs.
#   3. The user can disable or delete that provider at any time in AI & Providers, which
#      is the "turn off the app's own key and use mine instead" path.
#
# SECURITY — READ THIS
#   `BuildConfig` is not a secret store. Anything put here is trivially extractable from
#   a released APK by anyone who downloads it. Only ever put a free-tier key you are
#   willing to treat as public in these slots, and never a paid key or one tied to an
#   account you care about. Leave them blank for any build you publish if you are not
#   certain. A user's own key never travels this path.
#
# WHY TWO SLOTS
#   Free tiers rate-limit per key. The failover coordinator registers each non-blank key
#   as its own provider and rotates to the other on HTTP 429, which roughly doubles the
#   usable free throughput. Fill one or both.

# https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY_PRIMARY=
GROQ_API_KEY_SECONDARY=
